le=\"font-size:15px\">Dodge: **</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Larceny: </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stealth: **</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Bureaucracy: </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ride: *</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sail: * </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Socialize:</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Linguistics: </span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">GENERAL</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Virtues:</span></b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Compassion: ****</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Conviction: **</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Temperance: ** </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Valor: **</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Willpower: ******</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Essence: *</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Health Levels</span></b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1x -0</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2x -1</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2x -2</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1x -4</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Incap</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">X Dying</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Backgrounds<br /> - Backing (Temple Guardians) *<br /> - Contacts (Temple Guardians) *</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Merits<br /> - Special Sense: Spirit Sight<br /> - Strong Back</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Biography</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pakari is a Dreaming River native by birth, and only recently made an adult. Last year, he made a minor celebrity of himself by killing a dragon eel in a most unusual way - instead of spearing it on a flyby attack, he crashed directly into one, rode (read - clung for dear life to) its thrashing body straight down into the river below, and drifted along with the corpse into the fishermen's waiting nets. He nearly died, but surviving that ordeal gave him the reputation of being exceptionally manly and strong. The attention he gets for his reputation is a source of continual minor embarrassment.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The fact is, Pakari is built like a brick house and accustomed to being used like a pack animal - &quot;no need for beasts of burden if Pakari can pull the cart,&quot; or so they say, and Pakari does not object. He is content to lead a quiet life, following the orders of others and finding comfort in mundane tranquility. Never an ambitious man, Pakari is nonetheless driven to help other people he sees in need, and his (comparatively) prodigious strength enables him to do that.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pakari's mother and father both died of illness while he was an infant, so he was raised by Aroha, his mother's sister. Aroha brought him up to be pious, respectful of his elders, compassionate to all creatures, and to value labor for service and self-improvement. Pakari grew up doing enough labor for three people, which partly accounts for his build. After he &quot;wrestled&quot; a dragon eel to death (really, it was the fall that killed it, or perhaps the impact of Pakari's body on it, but nobody besides Pakari would let the facts get in the way of a good story) and became a man, Aroha suggested he find a more advanced trade - she believed that Pakari could do much more than be a simple hunter, fisher, or farmer - and when Hasya started asking around the village for a helper, Pakari was the first to volunteer. Now he wears a blue sash and carries the old man\u2019s belongings all around the island, doing his chores and occasionally learning a little - in the past year, he has picked up a small amount of herbal medicine by rote, and he is just about able to read. Pakari will generally follow his master's orders without hesitation, and rarely questions the reasoning behind any order.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Appearance</span></b></span></span><br /> Pakari is tall, broad-shouldered, and has the kind of dark skin that you only get from a lifetime of sun exposure along with short black hair and an understated mustache. He tends to slouch, as he spends much of his time looking down at other people or hunching under heavy loads. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> BP spending:<br /> - 4 BP on an extra dot of Stamina<br /> - 2 BP for a dot in Craft: Wood<br /> - 1 BP for a 2-dot speciality in Lift &amp; Carry<br /> - 9 BP on Special Sense: Spirit Sight (6) and Strong Back (3) Merits<br /> - 3 BP on another dot of Conviction - Pakari should be able to stand some hardship.<br /> - 1 BP on a Melee speciality in Fierce Blows (Exalted Core pg. 158)<br /> - 1 BP on a Martial Arts specialty in Grappling<br /> <br /> I have 3 Background points unspent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 08-18-2014, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T14:28:11-07:00","id":226354,"title":"","content":"Craft discount applies to all the Craft subtypes, so if you're going to be crafty it's a good idea to favor it. As far as sign language, I'd take getting your points across that way as a specialization, to allow you to communicate using pantomime and gesture. For a more formal sign language system, take a dot of linguistics. In the interests of making the world cooler, I'm gonna say that there's a sign language widely used in the Whispering Valley tribe. They're famous for being super silent warriors and hiding all night without making noise, so a good sign language fits them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T16:03:15-07:00","id":226498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign#post225772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mutations are subject to approval. No negative mutations for BP, though you're free to take 'em for RO reasons as with Flaws above. People of the Sea characters should take the appropriate mutations package.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a member of the People of Sunken Fires, and a shark tamer, I would like to petition for the following mutations:<br /> -Bioluminescence (Pox), West p. 152.<br /> -Shark Sight (Affliction), West p. 152<br /> --Otherwise, going on the picture in Scroll of Heroes for outer appearance: human, but with few fins.<br /> Currently working on advancing all pre-BP expenditures, as well as Sea Folk template. Will halt until granted/denied clearance.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, asking about 'professional Abilities&quot; would qualify. I'm thinking Survival, Melee, and Athletics, but professional dice might be covered as specialty dice instead, if we;re not using those rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 08-12-2014, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T17:31:25-07:00","id":226624,"title":"","content":"MG, if the hungry ghost obeys you, it should be a Familiar. That background is kinda terrible, so let's just say three dots (1 for normal animal, 2 for badass normal animal, three for minor spirit or magic animal, 4 for giant dinosaurs and badass magic stuff, 5 for things that are ridiculous awesome). <br /> <br /> Semi casual, Strong Back and Spirit Sight are fine. No to Jack of All Trades, and I am wary of Brutal Attack, I'd prefer you take specialties in combat abilities in things like Overpowering Blows or Pakari Smash or Bone-Shattering force to reflect this sort of combat style. If your main concern is optimization, don't worry about it. I suspect that a desire to actually hit stuff in combat is also why you're rocking Melee 4 without any training in combat or talk about how you're one of the most talented swordsmen/warriors of your generation in your tribe? I suspect some martial arts for grappling giant eels and maybe some specialties reflecting lessons learned from Hunter Tama in Survival or Stealth or Thrown might fit your concept better. You're going to mostly be up against low level opponents like wild beasts if you do end up in combat, and no matter how hard you twink you won't be a match for anything with charms that knows how to fight, so just relax and flesh out your character. A you're a mortal, Exalted is about being the desperate underdog and winning by the skin of your teeth here, so not being an \u00fcbermensch is okay, you can deal with all that if you exalt someday. I promise I'm not going to drop Ligier on you outta the gate.<br /> <br /> Edit: Please do not convert those BGs into BPs? If you cannot find a use for them, save them to drop on an Ally when you meet a spirit you think would make for a good epic romance. Floating BG is a thing that can save your life! If you are about to be eaten by the Mosquito Queen or a Raksha noble, being able to say, &quot;Hey, Guru? Can I blow one of my banked BG dots to take this thing trying to eat me as a one-dot ally because I make it laugh or it develops a crush on me or something?&quot; can be really handy. And fun, and sometimes silly in a good way.<br /> <br /> Brasstreader-Bioluminescence is fine, and it makes the People of Sunken a Fires way prettier if y'all can glow. Hell, it makes me wanna try drawing your character, bioluminescence is really fun to try and capture in a digital painting! No on the Shark Sight- dog trainers don't get super smell, shark trainers don't get electric senses. That's what you have trained guard sharks for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 08-12-2014, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T19:57:21-07:00","id":226721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=226624#post226624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Brasstreader-Bioluminescence is fine, and it makes the People of Sunken a Fires way prettier if y'all can glow. Hell, it makes me wanna try drawing your character, bioluminescence is really fun to try and capture in a digital painting! No on the Shark Sight- dog trainers don't get super smell, shark trainers don't get electric senses. That's what you have trained guard sharks for.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to try drawing him, that's cool. I'd appreciate it. Anything you need to help out? I'm partial to him being clean-shaven. messy hair ranging from chin-length to shoulder length, and.. some kind of gloves, so he can pet the sharks without grinding his hand on sharkskin.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T21:31:19-07:00","id":226779,"title":"","content":"Alright, here are Wahine's current stats (pending storyteller approval):<br /> <br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Savant<br /> <b>Profession</b>: Craftmason<br /> <b>Concept</b>: Wandering Artist<br /> <b>Motivation</b>: Find her lost voice and spread her craft works across the west and beyond.<br /> <b>Intimacies</b>: Cloud Hopper Haku (annoyance), marriage (trepidation), Sarika the Colored One (reverence and admiration)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Attributes:</b></u></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Strength: 2 Dex: 3 Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Charisma: 2 Manipulation: 2 Appearance: 3<br /> <br /> Perception: 3 Intelligence: 3 Wits: 3<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Abilities:</b></u></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Melee: 2<br /> <br /> Athletics: 1, Awareness: 2, Dodge: 1 Stealth: 1 (wilderness +1)<br /> <br /> Integrity: 2, Performance: 1 (stringed instruments+2), Resistance: 2, Survival 2 (tropical environments +3)<br /> <br /> Bureaucracy: 1, Linguistics: 2, Sail: 2, Socialize: 1 (non-verbal communication +1)<br /> <br /> <b>Craft</b> (air): 5, <b>Craft</b> (wood): 4, <b>Craft</b> (fire): 2, <b>Craft</b> (water): 1, Investigation: 1, Lore: 1, Medicine 1<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Finishing touches:</b></u></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Compassion: 2 Conviction: 4 Temperance: 2 Valor: 2<br /> <br /> Willpower= 6<br /> <br /> Merits/Flaws= Mute (4point version)<br /> <br /> Backgrounds:<ul><li>Resources: 2 (selling raw materials, finished works, or crafting services)</li> <li>Familiar: 2<ul><li>A very smart parrot with an exceptional vocabulary. Wahine acquired him when he was a very young bird and they enjoy a symbiotic relationship. He understands Wahine's signing and the 'human noises' he was raised around. He sometimes responds to or speaks for Wahine in simple or broken sentences. He is extremely playful but prone to mischief, especially on those outside of his small 'flock'. </li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Other notes:</u></span></b><br /> Linguistics: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>native language= Seatongue</li> <li>learned language #1 Barbaric languages: Whitestone Island and vicinity</li> <li>learned language #2 Sign language (west)<ul><li>Wahine knows a sign language variant of the western languages she speaks</li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>Wahine's possessions:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>Hand-carved Staff:<ul><li>The staff is covered in artistic embellishments. She uses it for fighting, hiking through the woods, and other utilitarian purposes. The tip can be fitted with a knife or other sharp point to make a spear.</li> </ul></li> <li>Pendant of Cold Iron:<ul><li>After gathering bits and pieces of assorted iron, she smelted a pendent to keep against her skin as protection from the Fair Folk. Within the pendent is the small iron bead that she clutched to her chest as a girl lost at sea. It gives her a sense of comfort and she believes it brings her luck.</li> </ul></li> <li>Other assorted possessions: hunting knife, thick leather work apron, basic tool kit, colorful carved mask (useful for eye protection when working), ukulele</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Personality:</b></u></span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Wahine is intelligent, clever, and resourceful. Although social situations can be cumbersome and awkward, she can be charming in her own odd way but the nature of her affliction can be isolating at times. She\u2019s a pleasant woman when she\u2019s doing what she loves and often has a smile on her face while she\u2019s working. But she keeps to herself most of the time and occupies herself with projects and hunting for materials out in the wilderness. A bit aloof at times, she keeps few aquantances and has even fewer friends. To those she's befriended or who have taken the time to get to know her, she is a funloving firecracker of a woman who\u2019s always up for an adventure. No doubt there's something </span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">magnetic about the artist. </span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">It\u2019s not unusual for an occasional passerby to watch her work, not just for the display of craftsmanship but for the blissful smile she wears when she pours her unspoken words, thoughts, and passions into her art. She often becomes uneasy during severe storms; her normal confidence </span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">faltering</span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> as she clutches the iron pendent around her neck for comfort and reassurance. Too much time immersed in village life makes her anxious as well.</span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> She much prefers the freedom of wild places and spends a lot of her free time camped along some stretch of coastline or unclaimed patch of jungle.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 08-18-2014, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T23:39:13-07:00","id":226817,"title":"","content":"I like her. What's up with the Virtues? Seeing an easily persuaded and dissuaded person with little self-control who is likely to give up on her goals when the going gets tough...with Integrity 3 is a little unusual, and Valor 4 means Wahine's likely to be pretty hot-tempered. Not necessarily problems, but I'm curious as to what sort of personality you're going for here. I'm having trouble connecting Conviction 1 and Temperance 1 with turning down Gaston and going on a quest to regain your stolen voice, y'know? Low temperance makes a certain degree of sense for a wandering artist type, I guess.<br /> <br /> Personality mechanics are, I hear, gonna be better in 3e, but I'd like to map 'em as close as we can before then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 08-13-2014, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T01:30:40-07:00","id":226844,"title":"","content":"Oops, fixed her virtues. Her virtues should more accurately reflect her character in a more mechanically sound, playable way now. (brave, gutsy artistic type who occasionally gives into temptation and vice but stays focused on her larger goals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T03:53:40-07:00","id":226892,"title":"","content":"Hey, Brasstreader. Quick sea folk character sketch! Can't make the damn thing link properly (curse you, tablet!), but I'll just put the URL below. It's a half-finished work. If you think it fits, tell me about your character's jewelry and glowing markings and clothes/tools/weapons and I'll throw some garb and detail and lighting on it. Good practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T06:01:52-07:00","id":226961,"title":"","content":"I adjusted my character sheet - changelog is as follows:<br /> - Moved 2 dots from Melee to Awareness - On reflection it would be weird for Pakari to be an exceptional fighter, but not so much for him to be observant.<br /> - Spent 9 BP on Special Sense: Spirit Sight and Strong Back<br /> - Spent 3 BP on another dot of Conviction - Pakari should be able to stand some hardship.<br /> - Spent 1 BP on a Melee speciality in Fierce Blows - it's a kind of Called Shot, trading accuracy for damage. (Exalted Core pg. 158)<br /> - Spent 1 BP on a Martial Arts specialty in Grappling<br /> <br /> I am leaving my last 3 Background points unspent, as per your suggestion. It feels weird to do that though - I'm accustomed to trying to squeeze every point. I guess I was kind of operating in the mindset of a different kind of Exalted game, where if you don't have at least one good combat stat you are both irrelevant and likely to die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 08-13-2014, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T14:08:15-07:00","id":227333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=226892#post226892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Brasstreader. Quick sea folk character sketch! Can't make the damn thing link properly (curse you, tablet!), but I'll just put the URL below. It's a half-finished work. If you think it fits, tell me about your character's jewelry and glowing markings and clothes/tools/weapons and I'll throw some garb and detail and lighting on it. Good practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>very good. Looking forward to the finished draft.<br /> I'll be done by tomorrow, myself. Anathema's acting up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T15:47:58-07:00","id":227382,"title":"","content":"Version 1 of whats-her-face the penitent, keeper of bones and general bitter jerk. Also, a child of the Dreaming River Tribe (whereas her yidak was a Green Flower).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Motivation:</b> To redeem herself in the eyes of the gods (not that she believes they\u2019re watching).<br /> <b>Intimacies:</b> Kusuma (Guilt), Shadowed Skies (Reluctant Loyalty), Tribal Elders (Bitter Indifference), the Gods (Resentful Piety), Hasya (Respect), \u2018Enoka (Affectionate Pity), Suanggi (Old Love), Jainat Marigami (Disapproval), Outcasts (Kinship), Kava (Inordinate Fondness)<br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Priest<br /> <b>Profession:</b> Mendicant<br /> <b><u>Attributes</u></b><br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 1, Manipulation 3, Appearance 2<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 2, Perception 4<br /> <b><u>Abilities</u></b><br /> Athletics 1, Craft (Wood) 1, Integrity 4, Larceny 3, Linguistics 1, Lore 1, Medicine 1, <b>Melee 4</b>, Occult 3, Performance 2, Presence 1, Resistance 3, Socialize 2, Survival 3, War 2<br /> <b>Professional Abilities:</b> Integrity, Resistance, Survival<br /> <b>Specialties: </b>Craft: Weaponry 2, Melee: Ritual Combat 2, War: Coordinated Attacks 1<br /> <b><u>Advantages</u></b><br /> <b>Essence:</b> 1<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Artifact 2, Backing (Temple Guardians) 1, Familiar 3, Influence 2<br /> <b>Virtues:</b> Compassion 2, Conviction 2, Valour 3, Temperance 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Thaumaturgy:</b> Dishonest (Creature)'s Rebuke, Spirit Sight, Thanks for the Hunt<br /> <br /> <b>BONUS POINTS</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>1:</b> Melee 4<br /> <b>2:</b> War 2<br /> <b>2:</b> Larceny 3<br /> <b>2:</b> Lore 1<br /> <b>1:</b> Melee specialties<br /> <b>2:</b> Craft (Wood) specialities<br /> <b>1:</b> War specialty<br /> <b>1:</b> Artifact 2<br /> <b>6:</b> Compassion 2, Valour 3<br /> <b>2:</b> Willpower 8<br /> <b>1:</b> Thaumaturgical procedures</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>NOTES</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Her Artifact rating represents assorted talismans (see page 379 of the corebook), as follows:<ul><li>An ofuda ward against goblins wound around the hilt of her weapon.</li> <li>A herb-scented rag, likewise wrapped around her sword-hilt, serving as a charm against disease.</li> <li>A full-circle pig tusk worn as an anklet. Carved with prayers to the gods, it acts as a good luck charm.</li> <li>Whispering Valley Tribe-style tattoos on her hands and forearms, serving as a double-strength ward against the dead.</li> <li>A ward against water spirits in the form of an ornate whalebone hairstick.</li> </ul><br /> Her Influence derives from her reputation as a witch or demon, and so mostly applies to attempts at intimidation. It's meaningless against those who know the details of her penance (Hasya, for instance).<br /> <br /> She speaks Old Realm in addition to the local tongue.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 08-14-2014, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T18:18:12-07:00","id":227460,"title":"","content":"So based on the fact that you're really good at combat and have Whispering Valley tats, assuming you were trained as an elite exorcist-warrior at the Temple of Eyes before being assigned to guard one of the island's more dangerous ruins? I like the char sheet. You could probably do with some warding or alarm magic, given you backstory, but the Guardians do work in teams so if you were the muscle and your former teammates were the warders/exorcists, that could be okay. Tell me about you ritual combat specialty. Are you thinking about duels, ceremonial combat for festival occasions, or what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T20:28:14-07:00","id":227557,"title":"","content":"Tinkered with Wahine's stats. I'm ready to call her done mechanically if there's nothing you want me to change or clarify.<br /> <br /> Also, how is everyone doing the spoiler button in their posts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T20:42:07-07:00","id":227562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxsimile</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=227557#post227557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tinkered with Wahine's stats. I'm ready to call her done mechanically if there's nothing you want me to change or clarify.<br /> <br /> Also, how is everyone doing the spoiler button in their posts?</div> </div> </div> </div>{spoiler}<br /> Text<br /> {/spoiler}<br /> <br /> but with exponents instead of curly brackets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T22:01:31-07:00","id":227582,"title":"","content":"well, I'm kinda got sick recently, but I'm going to try and post Seskan today :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T01:20:51-07:00","id":227706,"title":"","content":"Huelo Fokisi<br /> Attributes<br /> Strength 4 Charisma 3. Perception 2<br /> Dexterity 4 manipulation2 intelligence 2<br /> Stamina 4 appearance 4. Wits 2<br /> Abilities<br /> Martial arts 3<br /> (F)Melee (swords +2)3<br /> Lore 2<br /> Occult 1<br /> Bear.(criminal law+1) 3<br /> Presence(giving orders+1) 3<br /> Athletics (swimming+2) 2<br /> Integrity 2<br /> Resistance 3<br /> Sail 2<br /> Dodge 2<br /> <br /> Backgrounds:<br /> Resources 2<br /> Ally (deputy) 1<br /> (Remainder banked)<br /> Virtues<br /> Compassion 2 temperance 3<br /> Conviction 3. Valor 3<br /> Will<br /> 9 wp(9/9)<br /> Weapons<br /> Coral Navy Cutlass (chopping Sword)<br /> Billie club<br /> Other possession<br /> Small house<br /> Buff jacket<br /> Intemaces<br /> Rule of law(duty)<br /> Mother (love)<br /> Lost sister (love)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 08-29-2014, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T02:44:00-07:00","id":227723,"title":"","content":"Just edited the second post, put in a Cast of Characters (useful for me for keeping NPC names and relationships straight as the game goes on, hopefully useful for you too). I'm organizing most of the NPCs by their affiliation, since that social context is where you're most likely to encounter them. In getting up NPCs, I discovered I have a couple of questions which may impact local politics.<br /> <br /> 1. The MG, from your initial writeup of your character concept, you indicated that she was a chieftain's daughter who ended up training with the Temple Guardians due to criminal behavior to get her out of the public eye and to teach her some discipline. While she's now nameless and forsaken by her tribe and accepted only by the Temple Guardians, blood is thicker than water. If I remember right, you wanted to be have been born into the Dreaming River Tribe? That would make Chief Shadowed Skies your mother, and young Palms and Moon would be your younger half-brothers. That sound good to you, or did you want to ditch the disgraced-daughter-of-the-Chief bit of your backstory?<br /> <br /> 2. Hapless With Dice and Jen, I sorta wrote the recent backstory of the Sunset Tribe to give you two an in-Chieftain's children vanish (kidnapped by slavers), Chieftain goes into grieving and dies of illness, his sister's husband takes over. If Huelo is the son of the Sunset Tribe's former chieftain, he's technically the rightful heir to the position and has a claim to be the true chieftain. His mother and those few warriors still loyal to her would likely back his claim, but if his identity is known the current Chief and his supporters (and the Green Flower Tribe) would come down hard on a potential coup in the making. I know you want to do the law-and-order thing- are you keeping your true identity secret and building up popular support, or are you open about who you are and have publicly abandoned your claim to the throne and are serving the existing order? You two are kind of a civil war waiting to happen, especially if you're going to be trying to find out the truth behind your father's death (your mother insists he was poisoned rather than dying of a fever) and before I get too invested in that I want to make sure you're okay with that sorta thing.<br /> <br /> 3. Everyone Else: While character sheets are coming in, I'm looking at starting locations. I'm thinking of splitting the party into Eastern Island Posse and Western Island Posse (and maybe even a third posse, if things shake out that way), so we can get you involved with multiple tribes to get things nice and complicated. The downside of splitting the group is that it might take some of you guys forever to actually meet each other. The upside is that we can tell a slightly more epic story, with schemes and politics and adventure going on in multiple places at once, so you will have affected the other group and will have heard of them by reputation before you ever meet them. If we do go with splitting the party, I'd like to state right out that while I'm fine with inter-tribal warfare, I'd rather avoid PC-versus-PC battles during such a struggle. If some of you will be supporting the Green Flower tribe's goal of uniting the island under one chieftain, and some of you will be supporting a different tribe, I'd like to see you working to defuse the situation rather than just killing one another. If you all end up on one side of the conflict or if you are up against NPCs of the other side but PCs are not there, of course, the out-of-game exhortation to be peacemakers is lifted and you're free to get as bloody as you want.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure the Maiden and and Huelo start best either in the Sunset Tribe territory, which is their homeland, or in Dreaming River territory, as the chieftain there would try to build them into a wedge to separate the Green Flower and Sunset tribes, so she'd give them aid and local status and try to get on their good side. Hasya and Pakari are both Temple Guardians, so they could be stationed or traveling anywhere, and the same is true of the Bearer of Bones. Wahine is also a wanderer, but she's got an interest plot thread going with Haku in the Green Flower Tribe, and I'd love to get her in a party with Akoli Tane, who'd likely be in their territory as well because the Green Flowers do the most trade with his people. Seskan also fits well into Green Flower Territory, as his homeland is further west where the Wyld and its mutations are even more of a danger. Lyndon could show up anywhere....so...thoughts on where you'd like to start out and who you'd like to start out with would be good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T03:55:25-07:00","id":227737,"title":"","content":"I am building popular support first. It's the smartest route to take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T04:24:12-07:00","id":227742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=227723#post227723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The MG, from your initial writeup of your character concept, you indicated that she was a chieftain's daughter who ended up training with the Temple Guardians due to criminal behavior to get her out of the public eye and to teach her some discipline. While she's now nameless and forsaken by her tribe and accepted only by the Temple Guardians, blood is thicker than water. If I remember right, you wanted to be have been born into the Dreaming River Tribe? That would make Chief Shadowed Skies your mother, and young Palms and Moon would be your younger half-brothers. That sound good to you, or did you want to ditch the disgraced-daughter-of-the-Chief bit of your backstory?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still attached to the idea, but I wrote it under the assumption that there would be more and weaker chiefs, so...<br /> It would make more sense, I think, if she was a niece or cousin of Shadowed Skies, or possibly her younger sister. Given their relative ages (I'd place the penitent as a thirtysomething, having joined the Guardians in her mid-to-late teens), I think I'd like the last option the most, if that's cool.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, can we take a not from the Exalt chargen errata and take (Compassion + Willpower) starting intimacies rather than just (Compassion)? I have way too few of them, I realise.<br /> If not, that's fine, since I can just rejigger my BP expenditures to do the &quot;(Willpower) extra intimacies&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> (Also, Kusuma's a good name. I like it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T04:40:16-07:00","id":227747,"title":"","content":"Sure. More intimacies is more story-hooks. Hey, everybody, feel free to take Compassion+Willpower starting intimacies.<br /> <br /> Shadowed Skies' younger sister works great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T09:00:39-07:00","id":228012,"title":"","content":"Oh, I missed this post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=227460#post227460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So based on the fact that you're really good at combat and have Whispering Valley tats, assuming you were trained as an elite exorcist-warrior at the Temple of Eyes before being assigned to guard one of the island's more dangerous ruins?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was the plan, roughly. Additionally, she's kept her swordsmanship keen through various altercations with minor monsters and spirits during her seven years of penance, though certain other Abilities (like Athletics, and Presence) have faltered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could probably do with some warding or alarm magic, given you backstory, but the Guardians do work in teams so if you were the muscle and your former teammates were the warders/exorcists, that could be okay. </div> </div> </div>No, you're right. <i>Foretell Weather</i> didn't really satisfy me, so I replaced it with <i>Dishonest (Creature)'s Rebuke</i>.<br /> Of course, now I can't decide which creature it should apply against. Ghosts, I guess? Or demons?<br /> <br /> I also took the opportunity to change her talismans around somewhat, though the mechanics haven't changed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tell me about you ritual combat specialty. Are you thinking about duels, ceremonial combat for festival occasions, or what? </div> </div> </div>I forgot to include this, apparently. The idea was for it to apply when using ritualised fighting techniques and battle-chants against evil spirits, though it also serves for ceremonial combat.<br /> <br /> (I added the missing intimacies, too, including one towards Hasya.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 08-14-2014, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T12:21:32-07:00","id":228328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=227723#post227723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wahine is also a wanderer, but she's got an interest plot thread going with Haku in the Green Flower Tribe, and I'd love to get her in a party with Akoli Tane, who'd likely be in their territory as well because the Green Flowers do the most trade with his people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. I was thinking she probably uses one of the larger villages of the Green Flower Tribe as her home base. As the main power on the island, the larger Green Flower villages are a centralized location for gossip, trade, commissions, and odd jobs fixing things. There's plenty to keep her attention in the Green Flower territories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T12:35:05-07:00","id":228364,"title":"","content":"so I almost finished Seskan's sheets (except of the edited background section) and I managed to stop myself from creating more NPCs :P I'll try to post it tomorrow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T16:57:18-07:00","id":228564,"title":"","content":"Hm. If Wahine's got a kickass Airbender glider-staff, that's worth a dot or two of artifact, especially given your description of its construction. Feel free to take it without paying artifact dots for it, but rest assured that if you do do I am going to break the thing at some point, whether it be by storm or fire or jealous lover or hungry pterodactyl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T17:38:43-07:00","id":228579,"title":"","content":"*edit: I changed it to make things simple. Its just a regular hand carved staff that she sometimes fits with a knife to make a spear. I'll save my floating background dot in case something interesting comes up in game. But I like the idea that Wahine has developed a strong affinity for Sarika the Colored One and writes prayers on kites for the wind to carry to the spirit world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","user":"Foxsimile","date":". 08-14-2014, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T06:16:39-07:00","id":229015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=227723#post227723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">: While character sheets are coming in, I'm looking at starting locations. I'm thinking of splitting the party into Eastern Island Posse and Western Island Posse (and maybe even a third posse, if things shake out that way), so we can get you involved with multiple tribes to get things nice and complicated [...] ...so...thoughts on where you'd like to start out and who you'd like to start out with would be good?</div> </div> </div> </div> If WhileMyGuitar gets back before we actually launch, I'll defer to his decision for a starting location. Otherwise, I suggest that Pakari and Hasya actually start out in separate locations - Hasya can be doing shaman-y things in Whitecliff temple while Pakari runs errands in the Dreaming River village, stopping off to see his aunt and running into any PCs that happen to be there. Pakari's first goal will be to finish his master's business and then return to him.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:21:42-07:00","id":229393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0BzadX2FUXe05MzZ6RkhGM0xUMk0/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0BzadX2FUXe05MzZ6RkhGM0xUMk0/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0BzadX2FUXe05MzZ6RkhGM0xUMk0/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/file/d/0BzadX2FUXe05MzZ6RkhGM0xUMk0/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here's Akoli, version one. If there's more than needs doing, or if you'd prefer it written out, let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T15:18:17-07:00","id":229601,"title":"","content":"Looks pretty good to me, Brasstreader. Feel free to take some more starting intimacies, if you like, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T05:52:01-07:00","id":230110,"title":"","content":"Sorry for not participating a little sooner since I'm busy for the past two weeks with school assignment, here the Maiden's sheet.<br /> <br /> I'm will probably need clean up her backstory, personality and skill tonight.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Name:</b> Raven-Haired Maiden<br /> <b>Concept</b>: Wandering Doctor<br /> <b>Motivation:</b> To enjoy life and making people happy.<br /> <b>Intimacies:</b> Her master (Exasperated Friendship), Her Past (Cautiously Curious), The Future (Hope), The Audience (Joyful Delight), Her Performances (Professional Pride), Fashion (Leisure Pursuit).<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u></b>:<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 4, Manipulation 2, Appearance 4<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> <br /> I spread the Attributes a little more evenly after looking at other people sheet. Strength and Stamina is both at 2, with a Dexterity of 3 since dancing and performing need a nimble body. She's actually more of a shrine-maiden type instead of an actress so high Charisma will be need for those purification dance and harvest ritual; She has a Manipulation score at 2, Menreiki-san taught her the important of saying what other want to hear, but she's prefer to use her force of personality to convince people; Her appearance probably rate at 3, but years of brightening other people life have make it so that every words and action that she make seem to radiate an air of elegant and perfection, which explain why it got boosted to 4. Her Mental stat is pretty balance, though she will probably want to rise her Perception and Wit to gauge the atmosphere of social encounter in the future and change her tactic accordingly.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Virtue:</b></u><br /> Compassion: 4<br /> Conviction: 2<br /> Temperance: 3<br /> Valor: 2<br /> <br /> A High Compassion rating, the Maiden feel the need to bringing happiness to other people's lives so she can fill the void that is her past, whether by making people happy through mesmerizing dance and soulful song, or to remove their worry by performing auspicious ceremony that bring good-luck and fortune to a community. Her second highest Virtue is Temperance, the Maiden think her master is a talented but irresponsible person and which make it necessery that she's the clear-head and reliable one between the two. Her Conviction is average since basking in other people love has work at making her forget her past so far, she'll probably live until she die without even knowing who she was if not for the dream that she has been experienced lately. Valor rate at 2, not really a shivering coward, but she won't charge at a lizard tyrant to save the town either (though she will probably find another way to save it due to high Compassion)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Abilities</b></u>:<br /> Linguistics: 1 (Native: Whitestone Island; Other: Old Realm)<br /> Resistance: 1<br /> Investigation: 1<br /> Medicine: 1<br /> Craft (Water): 1<br /> Craft (Wood): 2<br /> Awareness: 2<br /> Occult: 2<br /> Lore: 2<br /> Athletic: 3<br /> Socialize: 3 (Interact with Stranger +1)<br /> Presence: 4 (Building Trust +2)<br /> <b>Performance:</b> 4 (Inspiring Happiness +2)<br /> <br /> Many household donate books and scrolls for the two of them, and her master make sure that she has at least some basic education, she's still dread to this day about all of his surprise exam. Old Realm is a must if you want to interact with spirit, at least that what her master say. She's also learn some basic cooking skill, some little recipes from a village's housewife, some little tricks from a teahouse's chef, enough to improvise when they run out of food. The Maiden would like to spend her free time to advance her skill at weaving though, she hate to admit it, but the Maiden love to dress well, she have encounter many wonderful kind of cloth material and beautiful draping style, but she lack the skill to make them herself which upset her greatly whenever her master mention it.<br /> <br /> The three social Abilities got spread out so I can improve it in-play. An average performer probably need some Athletic and Awareness. All those 1 Ability is mostly from her reading donated book when they're on the road, she know enough but probably will be beaten by expert in those field.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Backgrounds:</u></b><br /> Mentor: 3 (Menreiki-san)<br /> Resource: 2<br /> <br /> She don't even remember how long she has called Menreiki-san her master, though he can be a nuisance at time with his carelessness teasing, but he's the only friend that she has, and she will do anything to make it so that he won't leave her side.<br /> <br /> They could have Resource 3 if only her master would stop spending so needlessly, no, the Maiden absolutely did not want that beautiful woven sari with embroidered gem and gold thread <span style=\"font-size:10px\">:lie:</span><br /> <br /> <b><u>Willpower:</u> </b>7<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 08-16-2014, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T06:10:57-07:00","id":230121,"title":"","content":"Hm. A doctor? I thought being an actress was your primary thing. Medicine 5 and a Intelligence 5 and specialties makes the Maiden one of the foremost mortal physicians on the planet! How in the world did this amnesiac islander have time to go to Creation's version of medical school while traveling and spending her nights on stage and learning not one but two unfamiliar languages?<br /> <br /> I'm okay with Intelligence 5, if you are up for playing a character like that, but since it's a maxed stat and you have a couple of 1s in your attributes, I'd like to hear how your character's personality is shaped by these attributes. You're an actress with only Manipulation 1? You're a weakling with Stamina 3? Lots of highs and lows here. Lows can make for fun story stuff, but I want to see what it is you're going for, here.<br /> <br /> In terms of Medicine, I'm going to rule that &quot;aided by equipment&quot; is not a valid specialty. You might be able to diagnose without it, but you need equipment to treat a sick person in the first place: tourniquets, bandages, medicinal herbs, leeches, a brazier of incense to drive off the flu-spirits, whatever. This specialty would apply every time you treat a patient, it's too broad. Try narrowing down the types of equipment, maybe?<br /> <br /> I have to admit, I was sorta hoping for a social character here. We already have a couple of doctors and healers and shamans with medicinal training, I'm not sure going full-bore healer like this is going to help you stand out...what sort of story are you interested in telling with those medicine dots? Do you want your mentor /love interest to get sick so you can nurse him back to health? Do you want to deal with a plague outbreak? Did you take it because you want to use a Medicine to in investigate your father's death?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 08-16-2014, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T06:48:59-07:00","id":230145,"title":"","content":"@Wise Old Guru: Heh, I instinctively go for Int5/Med5 after hours of watching documentary about plague in ancient time, and mostly because I want to play a high Compassion character, and Medicine seem like the best Ability for that to shine, but free Performance for the children and the elder seem like a good idea too<br /> <br /> And yeah, I will adjust her skills into a more social role since I just realized that Ekorren's PC is already a doctor now that you mention it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 08-16-2014, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T09:06:00-07:00","id":230282,"title":"","content":"So, I have problem with my hand, so I can't write an edited background for Seskan which includes all the explanations for his sheets, so instead I'm going to just post them with notes which explain certain choices I've made. Hope you'll like it :P<br /> <br /> Name: Masagi Seskan<br /> Concept: Sacrifice Under Cover<br /> Archetype: Savant<br /> Profession: Thaumaturge<br /> Motivation: Start a new life<br /> Intimacies: Againa Lumami (Respect), Alial Daruma (Trust), Jainat Marigami (Desire to Impress), The Gods (Awe), the Huntal Brishmati (Fear), Bearer of Bones (Interest)<br /> <br /> [I'm leaving one free Intimacy after seeing if Lyndon and Seskan could be connected somehow. The interest in the Bearer of Bones is based around the rumors about her. He saw her ones or twice, but he never talked with her- yet]<br /> <br /> Attributes-<br /> Strength: *<br /> Dexterity: **<br /> Stamina: ***<br /> Charisma: **<br /> Manipulation: ***<br /> Appearance: **<br /> Perception: ***<br /> Intelligence: ****<br /> Wits: **<br /> <br /> Abilities-<br /> Archery:<br /> Melee:<br /> MA:<br /> Thrown: *<br /> War:<br /> Integrity: **<br /> Presence: **<br /> Performance: *<br /> Resistance: ***<br /> Survival: **<br /> Lore: ****<br /> Occult: **** (f) (specialty: elementals), (specialty: the Wyld)<br /> Investigation: **<br /> Craft (Water): ***<br /> Medicine: **<br /> Athletics:<br /> Awareness: ***<br /> Dodge: **<br /> Larceny:<br /> Stealth:<br /> Bureaucracy:<br /> Ride:<br /> Sail: *<br /> Socialize:<br /> Linguistics: *<br /> <br /> [the Attributes and skills represent his life as a Rakam and his trainings under Lumami. His Performance represent the way he use certain rituals, and his dot in Linguistics represent his mother language, the native tongue of Fankhou (his home island, literally meaning &quot;Dream's Gate&quot;)]<br /> <br /> Backgrounds-<br /> Resources: *<br /> Contacts (Temple Guardians): *<br /> Allies (Alial Daruma): *<br /> <br /> [2 Background Point is unspent. the Resources represent the small amount of money he gains in exchange for his knowledge in herbs and healing (and the rare times he use his skills is Thaumaturgy for pay, because he tries to hide the true extend of his knowledge). His Contacts among the Guardians are the result of his attempts in joining the Guardians, including one time he addressed Jainat publicly in the middle of a festival. While she and many other Guardians still don't trust him, it did has drawn certain attention toward him, including from the High Priestess. Finally, considering that he lives with Ailal and that he invest a lot of energy in order to help Seskan, I think he should be represented as an Ally]<br /> <br /> Virtues-<br /> Compassion: *<br /> Conviction: ***<br /> Temperance: ***<br /> Valor: **<br /> Willpower: ******<br /> Essence: *<br /> Flaws: Dark Secret (5 points)<br /> <br /> [Being born as a Rakam and living his life knowing that he is considered to be a tainted and that Huntal could demand him to sacrifice his life at any point didn't helped making him a compassionate person, while his life with Lumami thought him self control and to never give up. His Dark Secret represent him being a Rakam, which could end up with him being seen as cursed, being returned to Fankhou, getting killed or just ruin his life, one way or another]<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy-<br /> Initiate in the Art Alchemy:<br /> Initiate in the Art of Enchanment:<br /> Procedures:<br /> - Lesser Ward Against (spirits)<br /> - Spirit Sight<br /> - Deathsight<br /> - Dragon Nest Compass<br /> - Lesser Divination<br /> - Minor Changes<br /> <br /> [Seskan doesn't call the Art of &quot;Alchemy&quot; by that name, and instad refer to it as Herbalism, as his formulas are mostly revolved around using rare types of herbs, like Basil and Myrtus. His Enchantment is revolved around singing songs about great heroes and myths while writing the names of the gods using a special ink on the object, songs which include The Song of Changing Skies for Fading Color Treatment, the Poem of Shurabi the Old Maker for weapon Least Wonders and the Lullaby of the Endless Forest for Strengthen Wood.<br /> <br /> The Procedures represent the different Arts which Lumami has started to teach Seskan yet didn't finished. Lesser Ward is made by chanting an old song could the Clash of Two Flowers while using an incense made from Nerum, roses and lilies. the Dragon Nest Compass is a device made from a shining stone and a rope while singing the Chant of the Sleeping Blood. Minor Changes is a ritual which involves and old song called Lady in Masks and Veils while using a powder made from the feathers of rare birds]<br /> <br /> Finally, the two notes about his appearance- first, his charm. While he does his best to look like any other member of the Green Flower Tribe, he still keeps the old charm Lumami has given to him before he was sent to the see. the charm is a small talisman which looks like a clawed hand on an unknown beast, perhaps even a demon or some other spiritual being- and while the charm may or may not have special powers (for Guru's choice), the owner of the claw may still be alive.. and he may want it back.<br /> <br /> Second, his tattoos. Those complicated ink patterns cover most of Seskan's skin, like any other Rakam. Those Tattoos are inspired by an old legend which is told about how the Moon decorated herself with them in order to keep her madness inside herself and stop it from destroying the world. However, the tattoos by themselves have no power, and are simply a way to separate the dirty, tattooed Rakam from the pure, veil wearing Huntal- and which is why Seskan covers himself as much as he can when people from other islands come to Whitestone Island.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 08-16-2014, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T15:12:16-07:00","id":230602,"title":"","content":"I like him! Just to make sure, you do not get bonus points for Dark Secret. <br /> Also, Compassion 1 and you rarely take payment for helping others with your knowledge? You're doing it for popularity and to get in their good graces, not because you actually care? That's...actually in keeping with your Manipulation score, I guess. Tell me about your specialty in Elementals. It's interesting given that you mostly seem to be an alchemist and an enchanter. Did your mentor have lots of dealings with his local elemental courts? Is your knowledge academic or practical?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T20:36:00-07:00","id":230947,"title":"","content":"Brasstreader,<br /> You still interested in Wahine and Akoli starting out as friends? I'm happy to make Akoli one of Wahine's intimacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T05:44:49-07:00","id":231357,"title":"","content":"Yay! My first Exalted character sheets got approved! :P<br /> <br /> And yes, no BP got from Dark Secrets- it is simply that he has it, whether I write it down or not, so I decided I better to write it down. (and yes, you just described Seskan's way of mind up there- saying &quot;Here, take this medicine. No, I can not take so much money from you, I'm doing it simply for knowing it would makes you feel better&quot; while thinking &quot;Dance, puppets! Dance! Muwahahah!&quot;.. well, not exactly like that, but you got what I was saying)<br /> <br /> About the Elementals- first, yes, Lumami had dealing among the local elementals, for the Huntal don't allow the Rakam to make a direct contact with the &quot;true gods&quot;, and with Lumami being the highest level shaman and thaumaturge among the Rakam, he had a lot of ties with them (I thought about giving Seskan Elemental Sight because of that, but I decided that with elementals being the &quot;pinnacle&quot; of his mentor's knowledge he should have kept those rituals from his apprentice until he would be sure he won't mess up)<br /> <br /> On the other side, his Elemental specialty comes more from cosmological reasons- the other specialty is the Wyld, after all, and according to the teachings of Lumami, the elementals represent the innate order of the universe, opposed to the madness of the Dream (as the Wyld is sometimes referred), so while Seskan has saw an elemental or two in his life, most of his knowledge his theoretical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T05:40:41-07:00","id":232724,"title":"","content":"Here's what we've got so far:<br /> <b>1. Pakari</b>-Sheet Approved!<br /> <b>2. Hasya-</b>Waiting on Sheet (No rush here, player's notified us he's gonna be busy, may show up a bit after game has started.)<br /> <b>3. Huelo- </b>Sheet Approved! (Though I was briefly confused at your dots in Bear. It's Bur for Bureaucracy, for the record, though Luna has been petitioning to get it changed to the way you spelled it for ages. In terms of your sword specialty: the island doesn't really have swords, they have spears and arrows and blowguns and wooden war clubs studded with shark's teeth or shards of obsidian. The closest thing to swords if flint knives. Given that your backstory, I'm guessing the sword specialties were picked up serving as one of Coral's marines? If that's the case, and you've still got an actual steel weapon, it's quickly going to make you a bit famous. Steel is rare and a little bit magical around here. What I'm saying is hang onto that sword, it's got &quot;local legendary artifact in the making&quot; all over it)<br /> <b>4. Raven-Haired Maiden</b>-Sheet Approved (But maybe take a commonly spoken language if you've been traveling and performing off the island? Spirits love Old Realm plays but your average audience wouldn't understand a word she's saying in Old Realm or in her native &quot;barbarian&quot; tongue. I recommend Seatongue or Firetongue or Low Realm, depending on where she's been traveling...didn't you have Riverspeak in the first version of this sheet? Anyway, if you want her to have memorized her lines and acted 'em without knowing what they meant, with her Charisma and Performance and Appearance she coulda pulled that off, so no pressure.)<br /> <b>5. Akoli Tane</b>-Sheet Approved<br /> <b>6. Lyndon:</b> Still waiting on a sheet. (Ekorren's been busy lately, hoping still interested, waiting on a PM)<br /> <b>7. Seskan-</b>Sheet Approved!<br /> <b>8. Bearer of Bones-</b>Sheet Approved!<br /> <b>9. Wahine-</b>Sheet Approved!<br /> <br /> Tentative Starting Locations:<br /> <br /> <b>Calm Sea Village</b>, in Sunset Tribe Territory: Huelo is living here, presumably hiding his identity from all but his most trusted friends (avoiding Two Rivers Village, the tribe's capital, for a month or two now) when the Maiden's ship is spotted sailing in by the guards who watch the ocean for behemoths. It's also spotted by Wahine, who is enjoying a two-person glider ride with Haku, who is trying to impress her with a romantic flight over the island while she wastes a ton of her time looking up at how the glider actually works in the air and tries to figure out how to build a better one. It's also spotted by Akoli Tane, who is in Calm Sea Village trying to strike up a new trade deal-so far he's only dealt with the Green River Tribe, but he hears these guys have better stone and glassware...and because I can't leave you back in Green Lake Village all by yourself, Seskan, let's say that you've borrowed Alial Daruma's old glider and you've been practicing flying with it in preparation for trying to do the eel-killing and name-hunting ritual, and Cloudhopper Haku is keeping half an eye on you on your first solo flight...which should be eventful even before the huge fat foreign canoe shows up, given your lack of Ride and your low Sail skills!<br /> <br /> This first group is likely to split again once the Green River Tribe people head home at the end of the encounter to report their findings...but that might be a few weeks in realtime.<br /> <br /> <b>The Forest Near Dreaming River Village,</b> in Dreaming River Territory: Pakari, on his way back to Dreaming River Village to meet with his beloved auntie and to pick up some supplies for Master Hasya (who is keeping vigil near the Mouth of The Unending Scream, a cursed ruin in the deep forest where the wards were mostly swept away in a recent storm), comes across a camp fire where Lyndon and and the Bearer of Bones are midway through the process of teaching their languages to each other primarily through pointing and occasionally ridiculous pantomime, while a monkey sits nearby and copies them. I hate to make you two wait, so if it turns out Lyndon won't be in the game or won't be starting for a while, I can just have Pakari come across the campfire and have the two of them come across Lyndon in the woods later on (if he shows later on) or not at all (if he won't be joining us).<br /> <br /> Sound good? Any objections or suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T06:30:18-07:00","id":232785,"title":"","content":"I think it sounds plausible, if Ekorren and The MG agree.<br /> <br /> By the way, I just realized I never really described what Pakari looks like - he's tall, broad-shouldered, and has the kind of dark skin that you only get from a lifetime of sun exposure along with short black hair and an understated mustache. He tends to slouch, as he spends much of his time looking down at other people or hunching under heavy loads. Basically like<a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/InlM1lx.jpg?1\" target=\"_blank\"> Juan Aguacate</a> without a luchadore mask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T07:16:25-07:00","id":232805,"title":"","content":"Sounds good; let's do it.<br /> <br /> I kinda want to hear your thoughts on my NPCs first, though. I like the idea of them, but now that I look at them, they feel kind of divorced from the rest of the setting, so I think they're due for some revision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T08:10:21-07:00","id":232835,"title":"","content":"Sounds fine with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:55:13-07:00","id":233524,"title":"","content":"MG, I've added your NPCs to the setting, and I'm honestly sorta fond of them. Adorable little boy living in the Whispering Valley? Definitely gonna come up when PCs visit that place-which you will, because it's where some of the deadliest ruins are located. Crippled sea folk beggar (who rarely mentions that he's in the a Dreaming River and not being cared for by his tribe because they banished him for some crime he does not like to talk about)? Wonderful character, gives me an excuse to introduce some Pelagial-plot later on. Worry not! <br /> <br /> Got a couple of PMs today. Brasstreader is having computer problems and will be unable to commit to playing. I am hoping for him to return and join us when he gets a new computer and is once again able to do so, but for the time being we shall move forward without him. Ekorren confirms that Lyndon is still in, but his player is swamped lately, so it may be a bit. If I expect we'll probably move forward without him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T06:40:48-07:00","id":238146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=233524#post233524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MG, I've added your NPCs to the setting, and I'm honestly sorta fond of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Two things, though: 'Enoka is spelled with an apostrophe at the beginning (it's a glottal stop), and Suanggi isn't really that young - like the bearer of bones, she's thirty-something at the least.<br /> <br /> Oh! Should I note equipment or something on my character sheet? I've intended for the penitent to fight with a rattan shield and a sawfish sword/shark-tooth club (she makes one from whatever materials she can access), but I haven't really mentioned it before now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T05:30:14-07:00","id":239045,"title":"","content":"Oh, man, apostrophes? I guess I can accommodate apostrophes, but expect there to be typos and errors when 'Enoka shows up in-game and I'm away from my home computer and posting on my tablet...and thirties is still plenty young! Really! Suanggi insists!<br /> <br /> Noting equipment would be good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T10:16:19-07:00","id":239304,"title":"","content":"Aaaaand I'm back, haven't read the thread, really should get to it, but I am tired right now.<br /> Anyway, my biggest problem is that I do not own Scroll of Heroes, so can someone explain to me how one creates a mortal character? Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T15:55:09-07:00","id":239631,"title":"","content":"I PM'd you all that seemed pertinent and also not illegal. Hopefully that should be enough to make a character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=239045#post239045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, man, apostrophes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Be glad I used an apostrophe rather than <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%CA%BBokina\" target=\"_blank\">the actual Hawaiian letter</a>, which is <i>like</i> an apostrophe, but different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 08-24-2014, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T19:32:02-07:00","id":239798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=239304#post239304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, my biggest problem is that I do not own Scroll of Heroes, so can someone explain to me how one creates a mortal character? Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very similar to the core book rules on heroic mortals from what I can tell. The only real difference I can see is the introduction of mortal archetypes and professions. Mortals can fit into 5 general archetypes that function a little castes; Warrior, Priest, Savant, Criminal, Broker. Within each archetype, there are a handful of broad professions. If you take a profession, you get a small character creation bonus if you meet the minimum requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T10:35:35-07:00","id":241467,"title":"","content":"So.... who wants to go first?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T23:23:35-07:00","id":242860,"title":"","content":"I didn't realize the IC post was live. I just posted something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T00:04:43-07:00","id":242878,"title":"","content":"Sorry about that. Should have put up a post here to let everyone know.<br /> <br /> Expect a post from me in a few hours to get the second PC group going. Then I'm out of town for a wedding with spotty internet access, so not much from me until next week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T00:38:36-07:00","id":242885,"title":"","content":"No worries. I was out of town in NYC last weekend and am moving to another state on Sunday. Have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T04:51:22-07:00","id":243006,"title":"","content":"While My Guitar, you get all the relevant character generation information in that PM? If you have any questions, do let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:07:41-07:00","id":243233,"title":"","content":"Posted!<br /> <br /> I have a couple questions I probably should ask now -<br /> 1. How do we handle dice rolls in this game? The last time I did PbP game, it was on a dungeons and dragons forum with an integrated dice roller. Also, how do we know whether or not it is appropriate to roll? (For example - in the post I just made, would Pakari need to roll Strength+Athletics to move the tree branch, or can it be assumed that he can just do that? Would he need to roll Perception+Medicine to tell if the Bearer is unwell?)<br /> <br /> 2. Does anyone have any suggestions for polynesian honorifics to use?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T16:37:49-07:00","id":243486,"title":"","content":"2. Refer to older individuals as 'auntie' or 'uncle', even unrelated ones. Use first names when addressing those younger than you. <br /> Source I found for some Hawaiian etiquette. Maybe it will help: <a href=\"http://www.directoryofhawaii.com/general/general-hawaiian-etiquette/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.directoryofhawaii.com/gen...ian-etiquette/</a><br /> <br /> Admittedly my experience is in East Asia languages where there are complex linguistic structures for conveying politeness and respect. It doesn't seem like polynesian languages have anything close to this sort of formal linguistic system of honorifics and politeness. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T18:10:26-07:00","id":243510,"title":"","content":"I'll be away for the weekend, but I may turn out to have Internet access. If not, expect a post on Monday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T06:15:09-07:00","id":243839,"title":"","content":"In terms of rolling dice...generally, I hold to the &quot;only roll dice if there's a significant risk of failure or if failure could make for a dramatic complication&quot; option. Pakari can safely just move tree branches, his whole character concept is based on unusual physical strength. I'm not gonna make him roll for that sorta thing unless failure would be dangerous (maybe he needs to move the branch before some beast eats the person trapped under it) or likely (he's trying to move a damn tree trunk) or interesting (he's trying to impress a pretty spirit with his strength and failing complicates that attempt).<br /> <br /> In terms of rolling for perceptive stuff...I will generally describe the scene and show what's there, but feel free to make perceptive rolls at any time you want, and I'll add additional information and detail to suit. Feel free to roll Investigation or Awareness or Medicine to analyze your surroundings anytime your character is making a particular effort to gather information about them, and I'll give you more info.<br /> <br /> In PBP format, I generally like to avoid asking for dicerolls, because then there's a wait while the diceroll is made and another wait while I say what the result of the roll is. Feel free to make rolls on your own initiative if you think you've got a relevant dicepool (for instance, if Pakari wanted to do a dance to please the local forest spirits and get on their good side, you can just describe his actions and roll your social stat of choice and Performance-though please have a good rationale for the choice of your social stat-and make the roll without asking, and I'll give you the results in my post). Cutting out story-free OOC back-and-forth makes the game more fun and the thread more fun to read. Honestly, if I could just make Perception rolls for you guys and include their results in my posts when stealth or hidden clues or traps comes into play, it would be awesome for that reason...but I want to preserve your ability to spend WP or motes or whatever on those rolls, so they're one of the few times I'll ask for a roll and wait for the PCs to make one before responding.<br /> <br /> In terms of Dicerolling...been using <a href=\"http://dice.brainclouds.net/Login.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">this site</a> to generate dicerolls for another campaign, and I kinda like it. Make an account, make a campaign called The Whitestone Island Campaign, and use the dice roller to roll dice. If you have any technical difficulties, let me know, but it seems to be mostly straightforward, so it shouldn't have much in the way of conflicts.<br /> <br /> Formatting is like so: Make the short description something that clearly indicates what it is within the relevant scene. Make the long description include the math that produced that number of dice (Attribute X+Ability X +Whatever Fancy Mojo You've Got Going X=7), and note any extra successes (and specify their sources). Note them <i>within the long description</i>, not just the post, unless you have a Charm that allows you to add successes post-roll for some reason. <b>Make sure to check the 'Show die detail' box. If you don't, the actual die rolls won't be visible and the roll will be useless</b>. Embed the link (given in the html box on the right after the roll is complete) either in a mechanics spoiler tag (for combat and multiple actions and flurries and so on), or in-text if such detail is unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T09:42:03-07:00","id":244082,"title":"","content":"Wee, all the school-drama was over for me, time to sketch the Maiden and Menreiki ! And yes, he's a rabbit-ear man...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1]