title":"","content":"Holly Crap the IC thread was up a week ago yesterday. How did I miss that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T09:11:22-07:00","id":246183,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, I was not aware that Menreiki was a Wyld mutant, and we already have one animal-man on this boat.<br /> <br /> ...but on the other hand, he's absolutely adorable, so you can keep him. I'll assume for the sake of backstory that Menreiki was mutated on the same sea voyage as our tiger-headed captain. Just be ready for him to experience some major prejudice about those ears. The only local Wyld mutants are either servants of the hated Raksha or they're pariahs viewed as having been cursed by the gods with their deformities.<br /> <br /> As for the dice roller, Hapless, feel free to post the links for your test rolls in this thread so I can take a look at 'email and see what you're doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 09-01-2014, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T20:28:04-07:00","id":246578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=246183#post246183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand, I was not aware that Menreiki was a Wyld mutant, and we already have one animal-man on this boat.<br /> <br /> ...but on the other hand, he's absolutely adorable, so you can keep him. I'll assume for the sake of backstory that Menreiki was mutated on the same sea voyage as our tiger-headed captain. Just be ready for him to experience some major prejudice about those ears. The only local Wyld mutants are either servants of the hated Raksha or they're pariahs viewed as having been cursed by the gods with their deformities.</div> </div> </div> </div>He claims he's a child of Luna, jade rabbit on the moon and all ;-)<br /> <br /> Let hope those 3+ Charisma and Appearance score keep him from having tomatoes throw at him !<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T16:21:00-07:00","id":249269,"title":"","content":"While My Guitar, let me know when you're back and I can get a story thread going for you too. Hasya's currently at the entrance to a cursed tomb trying to get a hasty jury-rigged series of defensive wards up while Pakari brings him the ingredients he needs to set up a more permanent thing. I'm sure I can arrange for some interesting solo stuff for you until we get a chance for the others to meet back up with you. It may end up being wise for us to just have Pakari bring the Bearer of Bones back with him, if she's already got some of the supplies you need, so you don't have to wait for them to go back to town and gather stuff up. Plan was for 'em to meet Lyndon sometime soon, but no word on how long his player is gonna be with the real-life business before he can join us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T08:10:49-07:00","id":251491,"title":"","content":"Quick question, how developed is Sunset island. Do they have a sea port, do the tribe lives concentrate in one place or they're scattered around the island in small village ?<br /> <br /> And I wonder if other player can give me some kind of picture reference of their character. The Maiden's first impression with Wahine will be depended on how magnificent the latter's bust size is ;'D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T14:33:03-07:00","id":251712,"title":"","content":"Sunset Island is pretty much entirely uninhabited: it's dominated by an active volcano, and the people of Whitestone Island view it as sacred and only go there on pilgrimages in small groups, and they don't set up dwellings there. It's believed to be the home of Konani of the Evening Light, the local volcano god.<br /> <br /> Whitestone Island, the larger island, is the one the Maiden is actually from. They're scattered around the island in small villages, many of which are hidden from view by forest and mountains, but some of their seaside villages will be visible from the sea-lots of wooden houses and huts with thatched roofs. It is safe to assume that most of the seaside villages have docks full of small fishing boats, but the boats of Whitestone Island generally don't have much of a draw, so their docks are often pretty shallow.<br /> <br /> There are several sheltered bays where Phi Ho's ship could anchor, but you're going to find yourself drawn to the sheltered inlet where Calm Sea Village was built, on Whitestone Island's southern coast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T14:37:02-07:00","id":253599,"title":"","content":"Jen, I'd appreciate it if you slowed down a bit. In my post I indicated that the ship was half an hour away from the island, and that the captain was asking the Maiden for directions if she had any. The plan here is for your ship to get spotted by the other PCs while it's still at sea, sailing around looking for a place to anchor. Fast-forwarding into a seaside cave prevents you from meeting up with the other PCs. Also, I have not yet indicated that there is a seaside cave for you to fast-forward into. While I am fine with you declaring actions for the Maiden, taking control of the NPCs and the setting like this makes it difficult for me to do the whole Storyteller thing. Those sailors on the ship and the cook and Captain Phi Ho are my characters to play, and while I'm fine with you assuming some basic reactions for the sake of the story, fast-forwarding things and inventing setting elements is not okay. I can't plan a story for you if you go off on your own into a place I didn't know about beforehand where the other players have no way to get to you.<br /> <br /> Please edit your post accordingly. You've got a half hour to hang out with the NPCs and establish your character before you make landfall. I'm fine with your drawings or descriptions of walking on the shore if they're merely waking dreams or visions the Maiden is experiencing, but please don't zip forward in time. I started the story at sea a distance away from the island because there's things fated to happen before you make landfall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T17:01:15-07:00","id":253676,"title":"","content":"For those who are curious, Pakari's translated shopping list is 'Rope, ink, salt, incense sticks, and maybe bait traps.'<br /> <br /> I hope it's not too much of an assumption to say that the preferred materials for making talismans on this island are bone and white jade? (Bone would be cheap and plentiful, but Whitestone has more power, doesn't wear down as fast, and animals don't gnaw on it. In the absence of metals, these would be ideal things to carve signs and symbols in)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T21:16:08-07:00","id":253799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=253599#post253599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jen, I'd appreciate it if you slowed down a bit. In my post I indicated that the ship was half an hour away from the island, and that the captain was asking the Maiden for directions if she had any. The plan here is for your ship to get spotted by the other PCs while it's still at sea, sailing around looking for a place to anchor. Fast-forwarding into a seaside cave prevents you from meeting up with the other PCs. Also, I have not yet indicated that there is a seaside cave for you to fast-forward into. While I am fine with you declaring actions for the Maiden, taking control of the NPCs and the setting like this makes it difficult for me to do the whole Storyteller thing. Those sailors on the ship and the cook and Captain Phi Ho are my characters to play, and while I'm fine with you assuming some basic reactions for the sake of the story, fast-forwarding things and inventing setting elements is not okay. I can't plan a story for you if you go off on your own into a place I didn't know about beforehand where the other players have no way to get to you.<br /> <br /> Please edit your post accordingly. You've got a half hour to hang out with the NPCs and establish your character before you make landfall. I'm fine with your drawings or descriptions of walking on the shore if they're merely waking dreams or visions the Maiden is experiencing, but please don't zip forward in time. I started the story at sea a distance away from the island because there's things fated to happen before you make landfall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, I kinda suspicious with Wahine Perception roll that there gonna be a PC meeting up scene. I will edit my post accordingly.<br /> <br /> Another quick question, the island already has its own pantheon, but I kinda wonder if the tribe also worship the Incarnae, or perhaps they have their own gods for the sun, the moon and the star ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 09-10-2014, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T23:59:49-07:00","id":253872,"title":"","content":"The island's population does worship other deities besides the ones I've listed. Those are just the most major and popular gods on the island, the ones running the local spirit courts, who the other smaller local gods answer to.<br /> <br /> They do worship the sun (she is believed to be the mother of the world, compassionate but distant, who sails through the sky every day in her golden canoe) while Luna is often confused locally with the Ocean Father, and is prayed to by sailors looking to curry favors with the Old Man who commands the tides. The moon is believed to be a ship made out of bone and shells and gleaming with mother of pearl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T05:47:29-07:00","id":254030,"title":"","content":"In short just because you worship them doesn't mean you get it right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T15:12:54-07:00","id":254650,"title":"","content":"One of the downsides of being all remote and not personally interfering in the world for over a thousand years, yeah. Keshet, for the record, is often depicted as a great sea dragon who attempts to devour or capsize the boat of the sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T09:47:06-07:00","id":258244,"title":"","content":"It seem that our game move with a slow pace but each post have more words, which mean it's possible for me to make a doodle for each post o ho ho ho !<br /> <br /> So I decide to try my hands at sketching the Bearer of Bone on a whim, not sure if it fit with how MG imagine her ? Pakiri described her as a witch so I draw her with long hair at first, but I notice that she has an enchanted hair-pin so her hair turn into a messy tied crow nest in the end. And I suck at drawing feet, maybe I should be like Liefeld and use object to obscure thei character feet on panel.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should doodle Wahine and Seskan tomorrow since the two are about to meet the Maiden, I wonder if Foxsmile and LostLight have any more information on their character's appearance.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/imagejpg1-19.jpg~original\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T10:23:21-07:00","id":258269,"title":"","content":"Jen, here's a description that The MG gave me - your drawing is actually fairly close, except you drew someone much younger-looking and smaller than what I was given:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's in her upper thirties, crow's feet and all; dark-haired, but with pale eyes. Probably looks pissed at this junction.<br /> <br /> Her wavy hair is fairly short, but unkempt; she has the white-red-black tattoos of the Whispering Valley Tribe on her hands and forearms, though she's clearly not of that tribe. She's heavyset, and would probably be above average height for a woman if she didn't have terrible posture.<br /> <br /> There's probably a rattan shield somewhere nearby, and two makeshift club-swords of shark teeth and wood or sawfish rostrums. Her most obvious garment is a tasselled cloak or poncho patterned with the signs of the Temple Guardians.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T12:11:57-07:00","id":258355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=258244#post258244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I should doodle Wahine and Seskan tomorrow since the two are about to meet the Maiden, I wonder if Foxsmile and LostLight have any more information on their character's appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea where everyone has been the last week. Forum wasn't loading for me during the later part of last week and into the weekend. Anyhoo, happy to give a detailed physical description later in the day (I'm a graduate student. I'll be free tonight after I finish some work that's due tomorrow)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3560-foxsimile","name":"Foxsimile","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T01:39:16-07:00","id":258861,"title":"","content":"I just want to drop in and say sorry because I haven't created my character profile yet. I was planning to do it when I got back, but my life suddenly got very hectic and I haven't been able to sit down and write it all down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T05:38:36-07:00","id":259701,"title":"","content":"I've been around, but since I generally like to do big posts with a little something for everyone who has responded, it takes me a while to type one up, and I've been a bit busy this week. Expect a new post from me by this weekend, in response to everyone who's acted since my last one.<br /> <br /> Edit- No worries, WMG. Get it up when you can, I've got a starter post all ready for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T08:48:24-07:00","id":261275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/225772-ooc-exalted-the-whitestone-island-campaign?p=258244#post258244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I decide to try my hands at sketching the Bearer of Bone on a whim, not sure if it fit with how MG imagine her ?</div> </div> </div> </div>What semicasual said. However, that hair and those tattoos are balling, and are now canon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T10:33:55-07:00","id":261359,"title":"","content":"Dang, and I was JUST finished my re-done sketch of the Bearer &gt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/imagejpg1-20.jpg~original\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T01:16:16-07:00","id":261937,"title":"","content":"Okay, MG, you just made me crack up. Kudos. I'm enjoying the Bearer's dry one-liner sorta style immensely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T05:24:39-07:00","id":262039,"title":"","content":"I got a chuckle out of that too, let's hope that Pakiri won't become the butt monkey of the group due to his nice-guy-ness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T13:39:32-07:00","id":263055,"title":"","content":"I figure the best way to make sure Pakari isn't a butt-monkey is to make sure he's not a pushover. Comedic butt-monkey types usually suffer because they don't try to fight back at all, and I figure I can make him more assertive than that.<br /> <br /> Still, he's got minimal Charisma and Manipulation, and no dots in Presence, Performance, or Socialize. That's going to be a persistent problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T14:28:08-07:00","id":263130,"title":"","content":"I have no doubt that his destiny will protect him. Dating gods and shining as an earthbound sun is the kind of thing that cures monkeydom in a heartbeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T17:07:05-07:00","id":263266,"title":"","content":"Yeah...Hey here is a question...speaking of the shining thing...which do you think would be more fun. US picking our Solar exaltations or the GM picking them based on how our character's behave?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T17:23:47-07:00","id":263272,"title":"","content":"I vote for Wise Old Guru choosing, partly because I haven't given any thought to what kind of Solar I want Pakari to be and partly because I can't say beyond all doubt that my character will act like the caste of my hypothetical choice and I want his exaltation to make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T22:39:36-07:00","id":263475,"title":"","content":"Nobody's Exalting until 3E's been out for a while and I've had time to play around with it with mortal PCs for a while.<br /> <br /> If at some point someone does something I think is worthy of Exaltation, I'll PM the player in question to tell 'em I think they've just earned an Exaltation and what kind. If they want to play that kind of Exalt, it goes forward. If not, the Exaltation zips past them in search of some other candidate. So if, for instance, I think your surviving a horrible monster attack through sheer grit and determination could earn you a Lunar exaltation, I'll offer it to you by PM. If you don't want to play a Lunar, you can decline it and stay mortal, and hope that your actions will later earn you some other type of Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T06:21:00-07:00","id":265404,"title":"","content":"So, apparently The Bearer has no Awareness. That might explain a little about her history. Was that deliberate, MG?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T11:12:26-07:00","id":26